%N A402100 Numbers k such that psi(k) = phi(k) + Omega(k)^9.
%C A402100 The Python program available in the linked GitHub repository computes the solutions to the equation psi(k) = phi(k) + Omega(k)^m for arbitrary positive integer values of m. For this sequence, use m = 9.
%H A402100 S. I. Dimitrov, <a href="https://github.com/Stoyan16/Numbers-k-such-that-psi-k-phi-k-Omega-k-6/blob/main/A401783">Python program</a> (GitHub).
%e A402100 1255 is a term since psi(1255) = 1512 = 1000 + 2^9 = phi(1255) + Omega(1255)^9.
%o A402100 (PARI) isok(k) = {my(f = factor(k)); prod(i=1, #f~, (f[i, 1]+1) * f[i, 1]^(f[i, 2]-1)) - eulerphi(f) == bigomega(f)^9; } \\ _Amiram Eldar_, Nov 16 2026
%Y A402100 Cf. A000010, A001222, A001615, A401783, A402098, A402099.
%K A402100 nonn,new
%O A402100 1,2
%A A402100 _S. I. Dimitrov_, Nov 12 2026
%E A402100 a(22)-a(31) from _Amiram Eldar_, Nov 16 2026
